<node id="INFY.NS">
  <data key="d0">INFY.NS</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">INFY.NS refers to Infosys Ltd, a prominent multinational corporation that specializes in business consulting, information technology, and outsourcing services. As an important player in the global equity market, INFY.NS has a strong presence within the Asia-Pacific (APAC) region, where its financial valuation is reflected across various investment portfolios. The entity is not only recognized for its operational breadth but also for its attractiveness as a valuable financial asset among investors.

The financial valuation of INFY.NS varies widely across different portfolios, indicating its appeal to a diverse range of investors. For instance, it holds valuations such as approximately $160,458.12 in one context, around £180,360.94 and £10,990,049.50 in others, and notably 11,950,074.57 EUR in another investor's portfolio. These figures demonstrate the dynamic market perception of Infosys Ltd as an investment asset. In addition, INFY.NS appears in various investor holdings, underscoring its widespread appeal within the investment community and its significance as an equity investment.

INFY.NS is featured as an equity holding in multiple portfolios, including those of notable investors like Whitney Hicks, Amber Blair, and Robert Johnson. It demonstrates a variety of market values, such as CHF 1,977,105.34 in Jeremy Whitehead's portfolio and AED 390,669.07 in Amber Blair's. It also has presented valuations in various currencies including approximately 1,529,200.42 USD and other significant amounts in CHF and AED, showcasing its broad currency footprint.

The entity's status as a critical investment entity not only reflects its relevance in global and regional markets but also highlights its significance as a substantial equity investment within the APAC region. INFY.NS serves as a focal point for discussions regarding equity allocation adjustments among investors and during client meetings, further solidifying its prominence in the financial landscape.&lt;SEP&gt;INFY.NS is a stock discussed in client meetings related to portfolio management and performance.&lt;SEP&gt;INFY.NS is a portfolio ticker associated with the investment discussions in the client meeting.</data>
